T MotionIntegrator              | MotionIntegrator.h | 85-151 | owning                             | -  | Whether anything in the interface is still moving — the one question the wake rule asks. `DisplayScheduler` will otherwise present sixty identical images a second forever, and a UI that re-presents an unchanged image is not idle no matter how little it recomputed.
    has   InterpolantCapacity  static constexpr std::uint32_t          [-]  ?
    has   Springs              SpringInterpolant[InterpolantCapacity]  [-]  ?
    has   Eases                EasedInterpolant[InterpolantCapacity]   [-]  ?
    has   SpringCount          std::uint32_t                           [-]  ?
    has   EaseCount            std::uint32_t                           [-]  ?
    has   AnythingMoving       bool                                    [-]  ?
    by    Api/DrawerSpace.h, Api/ViewportSequence.h, Source/DrawerSpace.cpp, Source/MotionIntegrator.cpp, Source/ViewportSequence.cpp
    note  🔴 ⏱️ The genuine idle mechanism is not skipping layout, it is not waking at all. Under FIFO pacing

